  "hints": [
    "Two transfers from the same wallet at the same moment can both see enough balance. How do you make the check and debit one step?",
    "Money movements belong in an append-only ledger, written reliably even under a spike.",
    "Application Gateway (2) → API (8) with Redis locks (2); API → Redis (2) → DynamoDB; API → SQS → ledger writers (2) → DynamoDB."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 1656
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Lock the wallet (or use a conditional write on its version) for the check-and-debit, so concurrent transfers can't overdraw it.",
    "Record every transfer as two ledger entries (debit and credit) with an idempotency key, so retries never move money twice.",
    "Balances are derived from the ledger and cached for reads; a gateway authenticates every call and rate-limits abusive clients."
  ]
}
